In this strategy, manufacturers or other suppliers "buy-back" used products and components from their customers. The ability to predict return flows depends on the manufacturer's ability to set specific purchase prices. Hence, the manufacturer should define in advance what will be the desired stream between the entire product, components or materials of the product. Manufacturers need to determine the required amounts, price, time and sites of return for every form of return flow.

- For service and production purposes, manufacturers can obtain an inexpensive supply of components and materials;
- Buying-back used products may be an opportunity to reengage a new relationship with the customer for sale or lease new products;
- Deposition and incineration costs may be minimized;
- Understand how products are used and design better products.